  "summary": "MicrobeRT adapts three DNA language models to metagenomic read tasks, while metagenome-mining and typing methods appear alongside it as adjacent work.",
  "synthesis": "The one item with a shared-method thread is MicrobeRT, which fine-tunes pretrained DNA language models (Nucleotide Transformer, DNABERT, HyenaDNA) for metagenomic read taxonomy and resistance gene detection. This treats microbial annotation as downstream fine-tuning of general genomic foundation models, and it compares several architectures in one framework. The other two items are adjacent and do not use language models. NanoPAMDA addresses PAM characterization of Cas9 effectors from the growing body of public metagenomic data. HiSpoT is a one-tube dual-barcode PCR method for NGS spoligotyping library preparation in Mycobacterium tuberculosis complex. Both address how microbial sequence data are mined or generated for typing and functional characterization.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
